    95	The Enriques–Chisini sequence is the concatenation `M(β_0, β_1) ⌢ M(e_1, β_2−β_1) ⌢ ⋯ ⌢ M(e_{h−1}, β_h − β_{h−1})`, with the adjacent gcd-blocks sequential (not identified twice in the sum: they occupy distinct positions).
