293-· · · , a′ x + b′ y + · · ·) where ab′ − a′ b 6= 0 and the dots denote terms in x, y
294-of order bigger than 1. The map f −→ f ◦ Φ is an isomorphism of the
295-ring K[[x, y]]. Two curves {f = 0} and {g = 0} are said to be formally
296-equivalent if there is a formal isomorphism Φ such that f ◦ Φ = g · unit.
