991-We say that a projective plane curve C deﬁned over K has one branch at
992-infinity if there is a line L (line at inﬁnity) intersecting C in only one point
993-O, and C is analytically irreducible at O, that is the equation of C in an
994-aﬃne coordinate system centered at O is irreducible in the ring of formal
995-power series.
996-In what follows we denote by n the degree of C, by n′ the multiplicity of C
997-at O and we put d := gcd(n, n′ ).
998-We call C permissible if d 6≡ 0 (mod char K).
999-Let us denote by ΓO the semigroup of the branch at inﬁnity of the curve C.
1000:Since C and L intersect with multiplicity n at O there exists the n-minimal
1001-system of generators of ΓO .
