codex
A decisive hostile issue has emerged: the claimed “OPEN” scalar bound is actually false for general polynomial curves. I’m validating an exact degree-\((6,4)\) parametrization whose infinity exponent is \(15>14\); it also reveals why the residual’s \((6,4)\) gap count skipped an admissible generator. The example has an affine ordinary triple point, so it refutes Piece 2 as stated but does not by itself refute the nodal-only residual—there that row becomes OPEN, not closed.
